$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4,4'-Dibromo-[1,1'-biphenyl]-2-yl)(phenyl)methanone (2c): A mixture of
2b (1.94 g, 5 mmol), 4 (1.20 g, 6 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.17 g, 0.15 mmol),
and potassium carbonate (1.38 g, 10 mmol) in 200 mL of
toluene/ethanol/water (8/1/1 v/v/v) was heated to reflux for 12 h under
nitrogen. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, poured
into water, and extracted twice with dichloromethane. The combined
organic layers were washed with saturated brine solution and water, and
dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After filtration and solvent
evaporation, the residue was purified by silica-gel column chromatography
using hexane/dichloromethane as eluent. White solid, yield 86% (1.79 g).
1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.69 (dd, J = 8.3, 2.1 Hz, 1H), 7.64-7.62 (m,
3H), 7.49-7.46 (m, 1H), 7.34-7.30 (m, 5H), 7.10-7.08 (m, 2H). 13C NMR
(150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 196.6, 140.5, 138.7, 137.9, 136.6, 133.5, 133.4,
131.6, 131.5, 131.4, 130.3, 129.9, 128.4, 122.1, 121.7. LC-MS (APCI): m/z
416.9 (C19H12Br2O, calcd 415.9234).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
